# herdr keeps its running server's state beside its config: herdr.sock,
# herdr-client.sock, herdr-server.log, herdr-client.log, session.json,
# .plugins.lock. Whitelist config.toml rather than listing those, so state herdr
# adds in a later release is ignored without an edit here.
#
# This is not what keeps that state out of the working tree -- an ignored file
# still lands on disk. ~/.config/herdr is a fold barrier in manage/stow.py, and
# that is what stops the whole directory becoming one symlink into this repo.
#
# config.toml is a two-way file: herdr writes it too (`channel set`, the
# sidebar's sort toggle, `onboarding = false`), so expect diffs here that nobody
# typed. Confirmed 2026-08-25 on herdr 0.8.2: those writes append or edit in
# place and leave the surrounding comments intact.

# Ignore all files
*

# Except these files...
!.gitignore
!config.toml
